<h2>ATTENTION: ALL USERS</h2>

<p>A critical vulnerability has been discovered in the OpenSSL library used by our email infrastructure (<strong>CVE-2026-1234</strong>). This affects all versions prior to 3.2.5.</p>

<h3>What You Need To Do:</h3>

<ol>
  <li><strong>Update your clients</strong> — Make sure your email client is running the latest version. For Puffin users: run <code>puffin update</code> or download the latest binary from the internal repository.</li>
  <li><strong>Rotate your credentials</strong> — Change your email password and any application-specific passwords. Use the password manager to generate strong, unique passwords.</li>
  <li><strong>Enable two-factor authentication</strong> — If you haven't already, set up 2FA for your email account. Contact IT if you need assistance.</li>
  <li><strong>Report suspicious activity</strong> — If you notice any unusual emails or account activity, report it immediately to <a href="mailto:it-security@resistance.org">it-security@resistance.org</a>.</li>
</ol>

<h3>Timeline:</h3>
<ul>
  <li>Patches must be applied by <strong>Friday, June 19th</strong>.</li>
  <li>Systems not patched by the deadline will be temporarily suspended from network access.</li>
</ul>

<p>We apologize for the short notice. This vulnerability is being actively exploited in the wild.</p>
</div>

<p>Thank you for your cooperation.</p>

<p>— IT Security Team</p>
